license files. The current clients no longer depend on @assistant-ui/react.

================================================================================
Nebius Token Factory and NVIDIA Nemotron
================================================================================

ForgeFlow calls the hosted Nebius Token Factory API at
https://api.tokenfactory.nebius.com/v1, using the configured model identifier
nvidia/Nemotron-3.5-Super-VL by default. This repository contains API integration
code and configuration examples, not model weights or provider credentials.

Current official service documents (checked 2026-10-25):
https://docs.nebius.com/legal/agreement
https://docs.nebius.com/legal/token-factory
https://docs.nebius.com/legal/aup

The legacy Token Factory terms page states that the updated agreement applies
from 2026-09-28 except for the specified customers with an active reserve on
2026-09-15, whose legacy terms last until that reserve expires:
https://docs.tokenfactory.nebius.com/legal/terms-of-service
The applicable account agreement and incorporated model terms govern service
use; this notice does not establish which reserve or order terms an account has.

NVIDIA's official Nemotron-3.5-Super-VL BF16 model card identifies OpenMDW-1.1:
https://huggingface.co/nvidia/NVIDIA-Nemotron-3.5-Super-VL-120B-A12B-BF16
https://openmdw.ai/license/1-1/

Hosted inference and redistribution of model materials are distinct uses. If
model materials are distributed separately, OpenMDW-1.1 requires retaining
the agreement and applicable copyright and origin notices. The model card
does not identify the precise weight revision or precision used by Nebius's
hosted alias. Provider/model names and trademarks remain their owners'; these
references do not imply endorsement or relicense third-party material.

